  "reason": "The best result so far is config_032 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile, acc=0.7250). All four aggregation×fusion combinations for the scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile region have been tested, confirming transformer+weighted as the top configuration. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the transformer aggregation benefit (+1.9% over avgpool with ViT-L) is generalizable or specific to the stronger image encoder. Config_014 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted + multiprofile) fills the last missing cell in the resnet50 aggregation matrix (we only have avgpool+weighted=0.6776 from config_018). This clarifies whether the architectural gain from transformer aggregation is encoder-agnostic, which is important for understanding the design space. With only 1 experiment remaining after this, this is the highest-information experiment: if it approaches 0.70+, it confirms transformer aggregation is broadly beneficial; if it stays near 0.68, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is the critical factor. No untested configuration in the fully-explored best region can plausibly exceed 0.7250, so this exploratory test is the best use of the slot."
